import DocsLayout from '../../../../components/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Performance profile: where it is fast, where it is even"
  description="Where the zero-fork design pays off — command substitution, subshells and background jobs — and where external processes sit at parity with GNU."
  path="/en/docs/performance-model/"
  lang="en"
  enPath="/docs/performance-model/"
  zhBanner
>
  <header class="doc-head">
    <h1>Performance profile: where it is fast, where it is even</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The performance meaning of the zero-fork three-tier model (see the
      <a href="/en/docs/execution-model/">execution model</a>) fits in one sentence:
      <strong>wherever bash must create a process and niubash does not, niubash is faster; wherever
      both must create a process, the two are even.</strong> Every number on this page is a
      same-machine measurement (method at the end), benchmark artifacts ship with the package, and
      each can be checked on the <a href="/en/benchmarks/">benchmarks page</a>.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>Where zero fork pays off</h2>
    <p>
      Command substitution, subshells, background jobs — the constructs bash forks for on every use —
      are <code>ShellState::clone</code> plus an fd-table copy in niubash, never process creation.
      Same-session measurements of 2026-10-18 (750 iterations per workload, interleaved rotation,
      warm-up discarded, min-of-3, in ms):
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Workload</th><th>rubash</th><th>Git Bash</th><th>WSL (reference)</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Background subshell <code>( )</code> ×750</td><td><strong>1643</strong></td><td>2192</td><td>123</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Background wait <code>sleep &amp; wait</code> ×750</td><td><strong>1696</strong></td><td>1967</td><td>154</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pure spawn ×750</td><td><strong>1696</strong></td><td>2119</td><td>158</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Builtin loop ×750</td><td><strong>32</strong></td><td>40</td><td>3</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Foreground external command ×750</td><td><strong>37</strong></td><td>41</td><td>857</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <details class="zh-fold">
      <summary>中文原文 · Chinese original</summary>
      <div lang="zh-CN">
        <p>
          对 Git Bash 是 8 个工作负载全部占优；WSL 列仅作参考——Linux 内核 fork 让它的
          后台作业天然占优，但它的前台外部命令要跨 OS 文件边界（857 ms）、冷启动
          202–278 ms，且带走一整套虚拟机。迁移评估时，按你的脚本里「fork 密集」还是
          「外部命令密集」对号入座。
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>External processes: parity is a design fact</h2>
    <p>
      niubash does not claim faster external processes — they should not be faster. Single-spawn cost:
      rubash 1.183 ms vs GNU 1.121 ms — <strong>even</strong>, because both land on the same Win32
      <code>CreateProcess</code> floor. The entire zero-fork payoff comes from the "no process"
      paths, not from making "necessary processes" faster. That is also the essential difference from
      the MSYS layer: in Git Bash every process additionally pays the fork-emulation tax.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Hot paths inside the engine: gaps are engineered away</h2>
    <details class="zh-fold">
      <summary>中文原文 · Chinese original</summary>
      <div lang="zh-CN">
        <p>
          语言层的重负载也被逐个啃掉，而不是留着当「已知慢」：nvm.sh 这类重词法脚本的
          解析差距从 720 倍压到 8 倍（重词法字节量 −40%）；数组元素写入从 O(n²) 改为
          O(1) 追加——K=5000 时关联数组单次写快 45 倍、索引数组覆盖写快 177 倍；
          多行粘贴的自动误执行从 186 次降到 0（257 行载荷从 300 秒超时降到 4.6 秒）。
          这些不是理论优化：每项都有 PR 号与基准脚本可复现，夜间性能门盯住它们不回潮。
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <p>
      Summary in English: the heavy lexer workloads were closed one by one rather than left as "known
      slow" — the nvm.sh-class parsing gap shrank from 720× to 8× (heavy-lexer bytes −40%); array
      element writes went from O(n²) to O(1) append (at K=5000, associative-array single writes 45×
      faster, indexed-array overwrite writes 177×); multiline-paste auto-execution misfires dropped
      from 186 to 0 (a 257-line payload from a 300 s timeout to 4.6 s). None of these are theoretical:
      each has a PR number and a reproducible benchmark script, and a nightly performance gate keeps
      them from regressing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Startup numbers</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Metric</th><th>niubash family</th><th>Contrast</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>git startup (<code>git --version</code>)</td><td><strong>~14 ms</strong> (niu-git: MSVC + schannel, no MSYS)</td><td>Git Bash 45–103 ms</td></tr>
        <tr><td>One-shot execution <code>niu -c true</code></td><td><strong>26.3 ms</strong></td><td>Git Bash 71 ms</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Shell startup (5 measured runs)</td><td><strong>rubash 27–48 ms</strong></td><td>Git Bash 60–93 ms · WSL 202–278 ms</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Prompt git segment</td><td><strong>reads <code>.git/HEAD</code>, ≤29 ms</strong></td><td>Git spawned per prompt: 113–362 ms</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WinuxCmd tool layer</td><td>3.79 MB carrying 176 commands / 1,924 options, ~19 ms cold start</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Install size</td><td>niu ≈16 MB · zero DLLs</td><td>Git Bash 440 MB + 20 MB <code>msys-2.0.dll</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <details class="zh-fold">
      <summary>中文原文 · Chinese original</summary>
      <div lang="zh-CN">
        <p>
          提示符一项值得展开：Git Bash 兼容主题不 spawn git 子进程，而是直接读
          <code>.git/HEAD</code> 文件（微秒级），把「每敲一条命令付一次 git 启动」变成
          「不付」。一次性执行数字对 agent 与 CI 尤其重要——<code>niu -c</code> 的
          冷启动地板从 105.6 ms 一路压到 26.3 ms（一次性快路径六连 PR）。
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to read these numbers</h2>
    <p>
      Environment: Intel Xeon w5-3435 · Windows 10 19045 · same-machine WSL2 Ubuntu (GNU Bash 5.3.0
      contrast) · Git Bash 5.3.0. Method: interleaved rotation (rubash → Git Bash → WSL), one warm-up
      round discarded, min-of-3, identical timing for all three. Numbers move with versions; the
      methodology does not: nothing unmeasured gets written, wins and losses both shown. The repo
      also runs a nightly performance gate (per-asset timing trends; hard-fails over budget) against
      regressions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Full tables, raw TSVs and the runner scripts: <a href="/en/benchmarks/">/en/benchmarks/</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer class="further">
    <h2>Read further</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/en/benchmarks/">UNIXWIN benchmarks page (full tables + raw artifacts + method)</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://unixwin.github.io/niubash/why-niubash/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Why Niubash (official docs: contrast table and design argument) ↗</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/unixwin/niu-git" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">niu-git (the repo behind ~14 ms git startup) ↗</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/performance-model/" hreflang="zh-CN" lang="zh-CN">Chinese edition of this page</a></li>
    </ul>
  </footer>
</DocsLayout>

